<project xmlns="http://maven.apache.org/POM/4.0.0" xmlns:xsi="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema-instance" xsi:schemaLocation="http://maven.apache.org/POM/4.0.0 https://maven.apache.org/xsd/maven-4.0.0.xsd">
	<modelVersion>4.0.0</modelVersion>
	<groupId>io.github.ctgnz</groupId>
	<artifactId>jmsfx</artifactId>
	<version>2.0.0-SNAPSHOT</version>
	<packaging>pom</packaging>
	<name>JMSFX - Joint Military Symbology on JavaFX</name>
	<description>A JavaFX implementation of NATO APP-6E military symbology: a generated domain model of the standard, and the SVG composition that draws a symbol from it.</description>

	<parent>
		<groupId>io.github.ctgnz</groupId>
		<artifactId>jmsfx-parent</artifactId>
		<version>2.0.0-SNAPSHOT</version>
		<relativePath>jmsfx-parent/pom.xml</relativePath>
	</parent>

	<!--
		An aggregator, and almost nothing else. Everything that configures a build moved to
		jmsfx-parent, which carries no modules - so the shared configuration can be versioned and
		released on its own. This file answers "what is in this repository". See jmsfx#102.

		It does inherit jmsfx-parent, which looks redundant for a pom with no sources and is not:
		a plugin goal run from here - `mvn spotless:apply` being the one that matters daily -
		resolves against *this* project, so without the parent it fails with "Spotless plugin absent
		from the project". The version in the block above is not a maintenance burden either, since
		versions:set -DprocessAllModules=true rewrites it with the rest.

		jmsfx-parent also appears below as a module, because this reactor builds it. That is a
		different relationship from inheritance, and conflating the two is what makes this layout
		confusing to read.
	-->
	<!--
		Grouped by deliverable, not flat. jmsfx-tools and jmsfx-viewer are real poms because their
		children share a release; the libraries sit in a plain library/ directory because theirs is
		exactly the lifecycle that should not be shared - standard tracks the APP-6E standard, and
		each extension tracks its own domain. See jmsfx#102.
	-->
	<modules>
		<module>jmsfx-parent</module>
		<module>jmsfx-core</module>
		<module>jmsfx-tools</module>
		<module>jmsfx-viewer</module>
		<module>library/jmsfx-standard</module>
		<module>library/jmsfx-hallux</module>
	</modules>

</project>
